SCOPE AND THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
================================================================================

Original TypeScript runtime, development scripts, tests and repository-authored
resources and documentation are covered by the MIT grant above.

Third-party knowledge, templates, documents and native components retain their
own licenses. Exact sources, revisions, transformations and file hashes are
recorded in provenance/resources.json. DevEco Code attribution is reproduced in
NOTICE.deveco-code; the native Hypium components are described in NOTICE.hypium.
DevEco CLI template/document assets carry resources/licenses/deveco-cli-MIT.txt
and the corresponding upstream third-party notices. The CLI itself is not a
runtime dependency. Dependency licenses are supplied by their locked packages.

Official Skill definitions, upstream JavaScript executables and the former Skill
installer are not distributed by this architecture. Historical Git records and
installation fingerprints preserve traceability without executable compatibility
paths or changes to upstream copyright ownership.
